  "title": "BigQuery: Dataset Replication, Python UDFs, and Breaking Changes",
  "summary": "BigQuery introduces cross-region dataset replication and disaster recovery capabilities, along with significant enhancements for Python UDFs. Be aware of breaking changes where several job and replica statistics properties are now read-only.",
  "details": "This update brings several key features and breaking changes to the BigQuery API. Most notably, BigQuery now supports cross-region replicated (CRR) datasets and disaster recovery. The `Dataset` schema gains new properties: `replicas`, an array of `Replica` objects detailing dataset copies across regions, and `failoverReservationId` for DR configurations. To support this, the `datasets.get` method's `datasetView` parameter now includes `BASIC_REPLICA_METADATA_VIEW` to fetch replication-related metadata.\n\nFor Python UDFs, developers gain more control over package management. The `PythonOptions` schema now includes `buildConnection` to authenticate to private package repositories during build-time and `extraPackageRepositories` to specify additional Artifact Registry repositories for Python packages.\n\nBigLake Managed Tables get a new `metadataExportMode` property within `BigLakeConfiguration`, allowing control over metadata export (e.g., `ASYNC`, `MANUAL`). Additionally, `JobStatistics2` now includes `searchIndexingStats` and `vectorSearchIndexingStats` to provide output-only statistics for search and vector indexing jobs.\n\nBreaking Change Alert: Several properties across `JobStatistics2`, `Replica`, `SearchIndexingStats`, and `VectorSearchIndexingStats` schemas have been made read-only. If your applications were previously attempting to write to fields like `JobStatistics2.searchIndexingStats`, `Replica.creationTime`, or `SearchIndexingStats.baseTable`, they will now encounter errors. Please update your code to reflect that these properties are now output-only.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
